Task 1: hardening | Disable swap
Description Task 1: Immediately disable swap and prevent it from being enabled on reboot. Use the vault_hardening_disable_swap variable to control this functionality.

Task 2: hardening | Disable core dumps
Description Task 2: Prevent core dumps by adjusting PAM settings. This will set both hard and soft limits for core files to 0 across all domains. Use the vault_hardening_disable_core_dumps variable to control this functionality.

Task 3: hardening | Disable Shell Command History
Description Task 3: Disable shell command history for Vault-related commands by adding an exclusion rule in /etc/profile.d/vault.sh. Use the vault_hardening_disable_shell_command_history variable to control this functionality.

Task 4: hardening | Configure SELinux / AppArmor
Description Task 4: Configure SELinux and AppArmor for security hardening. This includes enabling SELinux, installing required SELinux policies, and enforcing AppArmor profiles for Vault. Use the vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor variable to control this functionality.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
- name: hardening | Disable swap
  when: vault_hardening_disable_swap | default('False') | bool
  block:
    - name: Disable swap
      command: swapoff -a
      args:
        warn: no
    - name: Prevent swap on reboot
      lineinfile:
        path: /etc/fstab
        regexp: '.*swap.*'
        line: '# Commented out by Ansible'
        state: present
        backrefs: yes

- name: hardening | Disable core dumps
  when: vault_hardening_disable_core_dumps | default('False') | bool
  block:
    - name: Set core dumps limits to 0
      lineinfile:
        path: /etc/security/limits.conf
        line: '* hard core 0'
        state: present
      register: core_dumps_hard_limits_set
    - name: Set core dumps limits to 0 (soft)
      lineinfile:
        path: /etc/security/limits.conf
        line: '* soft core 0'
        state: present
      when: core_dumps_hard_limits_set.changed

- name: hardening | Disable Shell Command History
  when: vault_hardening_disable_shell_command_history | default('False') | bool
  block:
    - name: Add exclusion rule for command history
      lineinfile:
        path: /etc/profile.d/vault.sh
        line: 'export HISTIGNORE="vault:* vault-token:*"'
        state: present

- name: hardening | Configure SELinux / AppArmor
  when: vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor | default('False') | bool
  block:
    - name: Enable SELinux
      lineinfile:
        path: /etc/selinux/config
        line: 'SELINUX=enforcing'
        state: present
    - name: Install SELinux policies
      package:
        name: policycoreutils
        state: present
      when: ansible_os_family == 'RedHat'
    - name: Install AppArmor package
      package:
        name: apparmor
        state: present
    - name: Load AppArmor profiles
      command: aa-enforce /etc/apparmor.d/*
      args:
        warn: no
      when: ansible_os_family == 'Debian'

