Task 2: Manage automatic service management
Description Task 2: Manage automatic service management for services installed via apt. This task includes a conditional block that runs when the package manager is apt. Inside the block:
- If apt_autostart_state is set to "disabled", copy a file to /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d with content "exit 101" and mode 755.
- If apt_autostart_state is set to "enabled", remove the policy-rc.d file.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook:
---
- ansible.builtin.import_tasks: assert.yml
  run_once: true
  delegate_to: localhost
  name: Import assert.yml

- name: Manage automatic service management for apt
  block:
    - name: Disable automatic service management for apt
      ansible.builtin.copy:
        dest: /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d
        content: "exit 101\n"
        mode: '0755'
      when: apt_autostart_state == 'disabled'

    - name: Enable automatic service management for apt
      ansible.builtin.file:
        path: /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d
        state: absent
      when: apt_autostart_state == 'enabled'
  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == 'apt'


